<https://iauarchive.eso.org/public/themes/constellations/>
    dcterms:title "The Constellations" ;
    dcterms:creator "International Astronomical Union (IAU)" ;
    dcterms:license <https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/4.0/> ;
    rdfs:comment "https://iauarchive.eso.org/copyright/ — “The images, videos and web texts on iau.org are released under the Creative Commons Attribution 4.0 International license and may on a non-exclusive basis be reproduced without fee, on the conditions outlined below.” The page is the IAU's former iau.org theme page kept in the IAU's web archive."@en .

<https://exopla.net/star-names/modern-iau-star-names/>
    dcterms:title "IAU-Catalog of Star Names (current edition)" ;
    dcterms:creator "IAU Working Group on Star Names (WGSN)" ;
    rdfs:comment "Footer of exopla.net: “exopla.net © 2026 The Working Group on Star Names (WGSN) of the International Astronomical Union (IAU).” The imprint (https://exopla.net/imprint/) states no licence. The IAU's announcement “New Star Names 2026” (https://iau.org/IAU/News/Ann2026/New-Star-Names-2026.aspx, footer “© 2025 International Astronomical Union (IAU)”) links this page as the IAU Star Names Catalog. Verification only."@en .

<https://simbad.cds.unistra.fr/simbad/>
    dcterms:title "SIMBAD astronomical database" ;
    dcterms:creator "CDS, Strasbourg Astronomical Observatory, France" ;
    rdfs:comment "The SIMBAD home page (https://simbad.cds.unistra.fr/simbad/, fetched with curl, query 13): “Use of SIMBAD service is free without any registration under ODbL licence. We request that users cite the original paper reference.” The ODbL (Open Database License) is a share-alike database licence that is not in the builder's licence list, so “unknown” stands in for it here; either way the source is verification only. CDS's acknowledgement page (https://cds.unistra.fr/help/acknowledgement/, read with WebFetch) asks users to acknowledge: “This research has made use of the SIMBAD database, CDS, Strasbourg Astronomical Observatory, France”. No SIMBAD content is reused in the deck."@en .

<https://docs.astropy.org/en/stable/api/astropy.coordinates.get_constellation.html>
    dcterms:title "Astropy: get_constellation (the IAU constellation boundaries as tabulated by Roman 1987) and coordinate transformations" ;
    dcterms:creator "The Astropy Project (Astropy Developers)" ;
    rdfs:comment "astropy's licence file (https://raw.githubusercontent.com/astropy/astropy/main/LICENSE.rst, fetched with curl, query 11) is the 3-clause BSD licence: “Copyright (c) 2011-2026, Astropy Developers … Redistribution and use in source and binary forms, with or without modification, are permitted provided that the following conditions are met”. BSD-3-Clause is not in the builder's licence list, so “unknown” stands in for it here. Verification only: the software computed values that were compared with the cards; nothing from it is in the deck."@en .

